    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8140" root="حشو" body-key="H">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حُشْوَةٌ</span></b>  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حِشْوَةٌ</span>: for each, see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَشًا</span>, in two
places: ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  and for the latter, see also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَشْوٌ</span>, in
two places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  You say also, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا أَكْثَرَ حُشْوَةَ أَرْضِهِ</span>
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حِشْوَةَ ارضه</span>, i. e. ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَشْوَهَا</span></b>  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَغَلَهَا</span> [app.
meaning (tropical:)  <i>How many are the thickets,</i> or <i>the
like,</i> that obstruct the tracts <i>of his land!</i>]. (Lh,
K, TA.)

